# 8. Convert the TCN into a dual-head model

Keep all existing TCN blocks and shared FC layers.

After the shared `fc2` representation, create two heads:

```python
self.return_head = nn.Linear(64, 1)

self.direction_head = nn.Linear(64, 3)
```

The forward method must return:

```python
return_prediction = self.return_head(x)

direction_logits = self.direction_head(x)

return return_prediction, direction_logits
```

Therefore:

```text
TCN → shared representation
              ↓
       ┌──────┴──────┐
       ↓             ↓
 Return Head    Direction Head
       ↓             ↓
 return          3 logits
                    ↓
              SELL/HOLD/BUY
```

Do not use a softmax inside the model itself. Apply softmax during inference/validation.

